# zurvan-eval: the candidate identity gets no outbound network at all (spec T3, defence in depth).
# pf matches `user` for TCP and UDP only; confidentiality never rests on this rule.
# Loopback is spared: the candidate identity owns the VM's host processes, whose control channel is ssh to
# 127.0.0.1; the guest's outbound traffic leaves through those processes and is blocked here.
block drop out quick on ! lo0 user ${CANDIDATE_USER}
